1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,861
Two agents, two worktrees, one file.

2
00:00:02,861 --> 00:00:05,801
Both pull requests pass against main.

3
00:00:05,801 --> 00:00:08,344
Merge one, and the other breaks.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,274
This is Bullpen.

5
00:00:11,274 --> 00:00:13,584
Source control for AI agents.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,571
One ask.

7
00:00:15,571 --> 00:00:18,712
The orchestrator splits it into three tasks,

8
00:00:18,712 --> 00:00:21,425
and three Claude Code agents walk onto

9
00:00:21,425 --> 00:00:23,638
campus, each on its own branch.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,622
Two agents want auth.ts.

11
00:00:26,622 --> 00:00:28,514
The first takes a live lock.

12
00:00:28,514 --> 00:00:30,474
The second waits at the door,

13
00:00:30,474 --> 00:00:33,042
and never writes a conflicting branch.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,940
The database agent reaches for the schema.

15
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,619
The referee, a Jetson on

16
00:00:39,619 --> 00:00:40,879
the desk, says no.

17
00:00:40,879 --> 00:00:42,699
The agent reads the reason

18
00:00:42,699 --> 00:00:44,169
and changes its plan.

19
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,029
Don't like what one agent did?

20
00:00:48,029 --> 00:00:49,517
Undo that agent alone.

21
00:00:49,517 --> 00:00:51,276
Its commits roll back, and

22
00:00:51,276 --> 00:00:52,899
the others keep working.

23
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,181
Happy with another?

24
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,543
Open its building, read the real diff,

25
00:00:58,543 --> 00:01:00,843
and merge through an intent card that

26
00:01:00,843 --> 00:01:02,459
says what changed and why.

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,111
Now pull the Jetson's cable.

28
00:01:07,111 --> 00:01:09,071
The referee is offline, so

29
00:01:09,071 --> 00:01:10,654
every edit is denied.

30
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,238
Bullpen fails closed.

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,568
Under the pixels, everything is real.

32
00:01:17,568 --> 00:01:20,067
Agents lock a file before each edit,

33
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,982
and the lock expires after ninety seconds.

34
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,627
Point Bullpen at any repo

35
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,319
and it builds your campus.

36
00:01:27,319 --> 00:01:29,077
Each edit becomes a commit,

37
00:01:29,077 --> 00:01:30,508
tagged with its agent.

38
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,879
It runs on your own Claude

39
00:01:33,879 --> 00:01:36,048
subscription, with no API key.

40
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,803
The referee runs on separate

41
00:01:39,803 --> 00:01:41,927
hardware the agents cannot reach.

42
00:01:41,927 --> 00:01:44,825
Small on-device models write the history, and

43
00:01:44,825 --> 00:01:46,821
a secret guard scans each diff.

44
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,364
Anthropic rebuilt source control for

45
00:01:50,364 --> 00:01:52,203
agents, and called it Scion.

46
00:01:52,203 --> 00:01:54,699
Bullpen brings that to every engineer.

47
00:01:54,699 --> 00:01:56,275
Git tracks what changed.

48
00:01:56,275 --> 00:01:59,164
Bullpen controls who's allowed to change it.
